        <briefdescription>
<para>interface variable has to be flagged Robin and elmt variable will be read as a matching variable placed on the element </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Constructor gets the finite element types that <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_num_integral__dudn__rhsop__u__d_s" kindref="compound">NumIntegral_dudn_rhsop_u_dS</ref> needs to turn the <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_inter_face" kindref="compound">InterFace</ref> into the equivalent of a volumetric element from the <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_finite_element_manager" kindref="compound">FiniteElementManager</ref>. Since InterFaces can either be triangles or quadrilaterals, their extruded volumetric pendants are prism and hexahedral elements.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="attention"><para>the variable &apos;thickness&apos; needs to be defined on the <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_inter_face" kindref="compound">InterFace</ref>, else the pde operator will not work. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
